\f1\fs22 Halo fought his way to the amenities corridor using a silver service tray as a shield and blunt-bladed weapon. Even the fury of the Elvi was no match for his fighting skill. As for the Airborne, they were too easy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The timing was perfect. Sarah emerged from the toilets as Halo entered the corridor. He nodded at her and smiled professionally; she reciprocated. They passed each other. Halo whirled, threw his arm over her shoulder and twisted her over his extended thigh, throwing her off balance. He muffled her cries with his other hand.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Off her feet and cradled under her assailant\'92s arm, Sarah worked her feet to regain purchase on the polished floor. She twisted her torso and grabbed at the attacker\'92s arms, but his shock-and-awe tactics had her off balance without leverage. She tried biting his hand as he dragged her, but the way he covered her mouth was too expert. Sarah almost panicked as she realised she was in the hands of a professional killer.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo felt her stop fighting, which seemed all too easy, but incredibly thrilling. Elation pumped his heart and breaths of victory filled his lungs. Everything was perfect. There was a hover-copt waiting on a pad twenty floors below. He was already savouring how he\'92d planned it. In the living room of a safe house he\'92d set up the perfect altar. A king-size mattress ensemble in the centre of the room was covered with a white, waterproof sheet that would allow her blood to flow and pool. Candles on black pedestals, cameras on every surface, an intricate array of belts and buckles and ropes and chains\'97all arranged just so. Tall narrow mirrors leaned against the walls, angled for every view. It would be perfect. He\'92d been diligent. He knew every dimension of every part of her body. Once strapped in, she\'92d be in the perfect position and at the perfect height. And with mirrors positioned by the edge of the bed, he\'92d be able to look into her eyes, and she\'92d be able to see the Point of Order raised then come down.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo awarded himself a smile as he pressed the call button for a service elevator that would take him to the hover-pad stalk. The doors immediately opened.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley\'92s first impulse was to call for back-up, then realised every Airborne in the restaurant would have their own private security on immediate beckon and call\'97immeasurably more effective than TRAMPS. But the Airborne were mostly bemused spectators. The fighting was almost exclusively among the Elvi, with a few younger Airborne throwing in for the sport of it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley scanned the room for Sarah. She hadn't returned from her comfy break.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo threw Sarah into the lift, stepped in and turned to punch the floor button for the hover-pad stalk. His satisfied smile faded when he saw her shoes on the floor, almost a metre away in the hall. He stood, frozen by indecision. His professionalism did not permit him to leave such clumsy clues behind. He tried to reach for the shoes without stepping out of the lift.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah recovered quickly, stealthily regained her feet and, while Halo stared at her shoes, hooked her foot in front of his calf and gave him a mighty shove. He tripped and fell out of the elevator. Sarah lunged for the door 
\fs18 CLOSE
\fs22  button. The doors responded. The attacker thrust his foot over the threshold; the doors jerked to a halt and retreated.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo regained his feet with the speed of a cat and launched at her. It was a feint designed to make her cower and give him the split second he needed to order the lift down to the hover-pad stalk. But she didn\'92t cower. Instead she stepped into his charge, grabbed his extended arm with both hands and twisted, using his own momentum against him. Halo\'92s eyes almost popped with the pain; it felt like she\'92d wrenched his arm from his shoulder as easily as pulling a wing off an overcooked chicken. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He dropped and rolled away, then swept his leg out and kicked her calf hard. She buckled and fell. Halo scrambled to his feet. Sarah thrust upward from the floor, fingers rigid, nails aimed like darts at his eyes. He turned his head just in time\'97her nails raked across his cheek instead, gouging shallow bloody lines from temple to jaw.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With all his might, Halo thrust himself fully upright and backed into the far corner, defensive stance ready. Sarah rolled to her feet almost as fast and backed into the opposite corner by the control panel. She slammed her palm on the 
\fs18 ALARM
\fs22  button.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo was running out of time. He growled and set himself for a proper fight. She had surprised him, but now there would be no mercy. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He came at her as if his life depended on it. He threw a jab toward her face\'97she blocked. He followed with a hook to her ribs\'97she deflected. A knee strike toward her pregnant belly\'97she turned her hip and absorbed it on her thigh. Every attack he launched, she had an answer for. And she was quick.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With the cold processing of a killer, he assessed his adversary as they fought. Even a little messed up, she was still beautiful and vital. The colour of her skin was perfect, her lips flush and full. She looked as if she could fight for hours and still be in perfect health.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Perfect health. What was it with this woman? Was there more to her than the intense attraction and the compulsion to have her that she made him feel? She was fighting him with such speed and accuracy\'97did she possess perfect reaction time as well as perfect health? Was she too fast and skilled for him? Who was this woman? Was she a woman at all?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo realised, as they fought, it was he who was taking a beating. Parts of his body\'97bone and muscle, organ and sinew\'97were complaining of injury. Then something in his knee snapped. It took all his training to remain on his feet.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With his dream of taking her artfully at the safe house fading, he took the Point of Order from his pocket.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
